1	diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
2	index b337aa9..37409ed 100644
3	--- a/README.md
4	+++ b/README.md
5	@@ -14,6 +14,8 @@ Fruit powers join the race (§9). Four fruit pedestals, two Ember and two Smoke,
6	 
7	 Every captain starts with a rumor (§3): an island where a rubbing type they lack is still sealed, or a sector with a recovery cache holding one. Press M for the journal: your rumors with why you got them (start, fresh, targeted, replacement, sighting), stale ones greyed out with what replaced them, the islands you have seen and whether their ruin is open, your types and your kit. A rumor whose target is emptied goes stale and is replaced; losing a rubbing in a duel gives a free fresh lead (§11); when every copy of a type is carried, the lead is a coarse carrier sighting, 30 to 60 seconds old. Moored at any dock, the journal sells a targeted rumor about a type you lack for 25 gold (Tab to its button, Enter), charged only when a lead is delivered. The sea shows its sector borders while the journal is open or a sector rumor is active.
8	 
9	+Gold makes route choices (§11). Four supply crates float along the routes between the islands and the hub: the first ship to touch one takes its 25 gold, and it is gone for everyone. Moored at any dock, B opens the shop: a sail tonic for 30 gold (carry at most two) and the journal's targeted rumors. At sea, T drinks a tonic: +10 % top speed (39 → 43 sub-units a tick) for 12 seconds, with a timer in the purse; not while moored, grappled, in a duel or while one works, and a lost duel keeps your tonics. The shop is no safe zone: a moored ship can still be grappled. Holding E or F survives short network stalls (up to about half a second); letting go ends the hold at once.
10	+
11	 The standalone duel (the combat spike, §18 stage 1) runs beside it: "Create duel" makes a 1v1 duel whose code the second browser enters under "Join duel", and "Practice" fights a server-side dummy (idle or guarding). After a three-second countdown both browsers predict the fight with the shared duel simulation and roll back to the server's inputs (`docs/duel.md`). Keys (§8): WASD or the arrows move (hold back to guard), J light, K heavy, U and I specials, Shift dash, J and K together throw. The HUD shows both health bars, stamina, the round clock, the connection line (round trip, input delay, corrections) and the result; "Show hitboxes" draws hurtboxes and active hitboxes.
12	 
13	 ## Requirements
